# Mood Palette — Visual Mood Tracker (Tkinter App)

**What does it do?**

Mood Palette is an innovative desktop GUI tool that helps you track your daily moods visually using colors. Each day you select your current feeling from preset moods (or create your own) and assign it to today's date with an associated color. The app displays these entries as colored tiles on a monthly calendar grid—so over time you get an instant visual overview of how you've been feeling.

**Features**
- Modern minimalist interface with professional fonts/colors.
- Add today's mood quickly via button.
- Hover over any day's tile to see details about the selected mood/date.
- Export/import data easily as JSON files so you never lose your history.

**How does it work?**
1. Launch the application (`python mood_palette.py`).
2. Click 'Add Today's Mood' to select how you're feeling today; pick from suggested moods/colors or enter custom ones!
3. Your selection appears instantly on this month's calendar view—a new colored square per day!
4. Hover over any square to review what was entered that day.
5. Use 'Export Data' anytime to save all entries safely.

This tool makes emotional tracking fun—and beautiful!

*Requires Python 3.x.*
